# Discovery cycle completion

A cycle is complete only when this run saved at least one new qualifying store.

- Never show "finished", "cycle finished", or equivalent success-complete copy unless that happened.
- If sources were empty, blocked, all duplicates, robots-denied, or below the freshness bar, the cycle did not complete. Say that. Point to the activity log and Rejected candidates.
- Check every website the user asked for. A run of 100 checks 100. A run of 1,000 checks 1,000. Saving a qualifying store does not stop the run early. Stop only when that count is checked or every available source is exhausted.
- Do not treat leftover leads from an earlier run as proof this cycle succeeded.
- Once a website is checked in any cycle, never include it in a later cycle. Skip it permanently, even if public sources list it again.
- Do not ask the user to paste store URLs.
- Do not invent launch dates. "Found today" is not "launched today."
- A qualifying lead needs all three: a public business email, a country the store publishes that matches the selected countries, and public proof the store appeared within the new-store window. Found today is not launched today. Homepage launch wording, a certificate renewal, and an old domain are rejected. Missing email or country goes to rejected.
- Country filters use only a country the storefront publishes. Never infer country from Shopify CDN IPs, urlscan scanner location, or a myshopify.com hostname.
- Public data only. Respect robots.txt on storefronts. No admin, CAPTCHA, or auth bypass.
